## 2. The `.txg` Specification (v0.2.0)

### A. Grammar (EBNF Snippet)
```ebnf
document  = { NL | comment | directive | statement } ;
directive = "@" NAME ":" ( STRING | TEXT ) NL ;   (* @txg must be first *)
statement = ( reads | flow ) [ comment ] ( NL | EOF ) ;

reads     = node "reads" ":" node { "," node } ;
flow      = node chain ;
chain     = { edge ( node | fork ) } ;
edge      = "->" | "-!>" ;                        (* standard | fallback *)
bound     = "(" "loop" "max" INT [ "," "carry" ":" ID {"," ID} ] ")" ;
fork      = "?" test "{" arm { ( NL | "," ) arm } "}" ;
test      = "exit" [ "(" ID ")" ] | "judge" STRING ;
arm       = pattern "=>" node [ chain ] ;
pattern   = INT | STRING | "_" ;
```

### B. Diagnostic Suite (TXG001–TXG025)
| ID | Severity | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| **TXG001** | error | Lexical/Parse error (e.g., bad escape, unterminated string). |
| **TXG002** | error | Missing `@txg` or major version mismatch (hard exit). |
| **TXG003** | error | Duplicate node ID declaration. |
| **TXG004** | error | Undeclared bare ID reference. |
| **TXG005** | error | Bound on non-header, OR back-edge into a header without a bound. |
| **TXG006** | error | `? exit` fork with no preceding `tool:` in the execution scope. |
| **TXG007** | warn | Fork is missing the `_` fallback arm. |
| **TXG008** | error | Unresolvable ref: `missing-file`, `label-into-reads`, `invalid-carry-source`. |
| **TXG009** | warn | Orphan assets in `references/` or `scripts/` not referenced by any node. |
| **TXG010** | error | `tool:` invocation missing from `SKILL.md` frontmatter permissions. |
| **TXG011** | warn | Unknown directive, invalid `@token_ratio` (1-8), or malformed budget. |
| **TXG012** | error | Unknown box kind (e.g., `[script: ...]`). |
| **TXG013** | error | Duplicate annotations, or `(idempotent)` on a non-`tool:` node. |
| **TXG014** | error | `[ask:]` requires a non-empty STRING payload. |
| **TXG015** | error | Path containment failure (absolute, drive letter, or `..`). |
| **TXG016** | error | Duplicate pattern in a fork (e.g., two `0 =>` arms). |
| **TXG017** | warn | Unreachable arm positioned after `_`. |
| **TXG018** | warn | `carry:` source does not dominate all back-edges into the loop header. |
| **TXG019** | error | Irreducible control flow (SCC with multiple entry headers). |
| **TXG020** | warn | Node has zero out-degree and is not `[halt]` (dangling leaf). |
| **TXG021** | warn | Bounded loop traverses a `tool:` lacking `(idempotent)`. |
| **TXG022** | warn/error | Bounded header lacks `-!>`. (Warn if plain loop, **Error** if `carry:`). |
| **TXG023** | warn/error | Budget exceeded. Warn @ 0.8x, Error @ 1.0x. (`peak-turn` or `peak-iteration`). |
| **TXG024** | warn | Node is unreachable from `@entry`/statement starts. |
| **TXG025** | error | `@txg` present but not the first directive. |

