## 3. Architectural Discoveries & Ratifications (R-Series)

During the development and dual-language verification, the following bugs, gaps, and semantic refinements were discovered and locked:

*   **[R14] Fat Arrow Lexing:** `=>` was initially missing from the lexer. All forks would fail. Patched in both Python and JS.
*   **[R23] Multi-line Annotations:** `parse_annotations` failed if a `(loop max...)` was on a newline. Fixed by adding save-and-restore newline skipping.
*   **[R24b] Single-Statement Headers:** SCC entry detection failed for self-loops (`h -> h`). Fixed by falling back to the statement's root node inside the SCC.
*   **[R30] Frontmatter YAML Subset:** `SKILL.md` permissions are strictly `allowed_tools:` or `permissions:` with `- ` or `[a, b]` lists.
*   **[R31] Missing `SKILL.md`:** If absent, permission checks (TXG010) are bypassed entirely.
*   **[R32] Tarjan & Fork Delimiters:** Standard Tarjan dropped single-node self-loops; patched to detect `len(scc) == 1 and v in edges[v]`. Fork arm parsing was consuming the newline separating arms; patched by skipping Nls before checking for `}`.

